(CVE-2026-1757) Memory leak in xmllint Shell - shell.c

Summary

There is a memory leak issue in the command parsing logic of the xmllint interactive shell. After entering spaces of any length in the shell and then typing the quit command to exit, you can see the memory leak information output by ASAN. If you enter enough lines of spaces, it will exhaust the entire system's memory, cause the program to crash, and trigger a Denial of Service (DoS).

Poc

echo ' ' | ./xmllint --shell test.xml

ASAN Output:

/ > / > 
=================================================================
==1200505==ERROR: LeakSanitizer: detected memory leaks

Direct leak of 3 byte(s) in 1 object(s) allocated from:
    #0 0x7d32044b4887 in __interceptor_malloc ../../../../src/libsanitizer/asan/asan_malloc_linux.cpp:145
    #1 0x5a53bd1f3be1 in xmllintShellReadline /home/yl/PHDlife/CProjects/libxml2/shell.c:1055
    #2 0x5a53bd1f4510 in xmllintShell /home/yl/PHDlife/CProjects/libxml2/shell.c:1122
    #3 0x5a53bd1e4197 in parseAndPrintFile /home/yl/PHDlife/CProjects/libxml2/xmllint.c:1858
    #4 0x5a53bd1efa12 in xmllintMain /home/yl/PHDlife/CProjects/libxml2/xmllint.c:3263
    #5 0x5a53bd1f81c7 in main /home/yl/PHDlife/CProjects/libxml2/lintmain.c:13
    #6 0x7d3203229d8f in __libc_start_call_main ../sysdeps/nptl/libc_start_call_main.h:58

SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 3 byte(s) leaked in 1 allocation(s).

Analysis

If cmdline consists entirely of spaces, the program will first skip all whitespace characters, then fail to extract a command name, and finally determine the command is empty before executing continue. The program will ignore this all-space input, return directly to the start of the loop, and re-call xmllintShellReadline(prompt) to wait for the next input. No actual operations will be performed. However, at this point, the memory allocated for cmdline has not been freed yet when the program proceeds to the next loop iteration.

void
xmllintShell(xmlDoc *doc, const char *filename, FILE * output){
    [...]
    cmdline = xmllintShellReadline(prompt);
    if (cmdline == NULL)
        break;

    /*
     * Parse the command itself
     */
    cur = cmdline;
    while ((*cur == ' ') || (*cur == '\t'))
        cur++;
    i = 0;
    while ((*cur != ' ') && (*cur != '\t') &&
           (*cur != '\n') && (*cur != '\r') &&
           (i < (MAX_COMMAND_SIZE - 1))) {
        if (*cur == 0)
            break;
        command[i++] = *cur++;
    }
    command[i] = 0;
    if (i == 0)
        continue;  # no free(cmdline) before continue
    [...]
}

Suggestion Fix

Manually free the memory pointed to by cmdline before executing continue.

if (i == 0) {
    free(cmdline);
    continue;
}

If possible, I would like to request a CVE ID.

